    "id": 240,
    "text": "Write about IUDs and its types",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Demography and Family Planning",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### INTRAUTERINE DEVICES (IUDs) AND THEIR TYPES\n\n### A) DEFINITION AND OVERVIEW\nAn Intrauterine Device (IUD) is a highly effective, long-acting reversible contraceptive (LARC) device inserted into the uterine cavity by a trained healthcare professional (doctor or nurse) during menstruation or immediately post-partum. IUDs are the most widely used reversible method of spacing pregnancies globally.\n\n---\n\n### B) CLASSIFICATION OF IUDs (THREE GENERATIONS)\n\n#### 1. First-Generation IUDs (Non-Medicated / Inert)\n* **Description**: Made of non-reactive polyethylene or other inert materials, available in various shapes and sizes.\n* **Mechanism**: Act simply as a mechanical foreign body, producing a local aseptic inflammatory reaction in the endometrium that prevents implantation.\n* **Example**: **Lippes Loop** (a double-S-shaped plastic device).\n* **Current Status**: Largely obsolete and replaced by newer, more effective medicated devices, but could remain in the uterus indefinitely if well-tolerated.\n\n#### 2. Second-Generation IUDs (Medicated / Copper-Releasing)\n* **Description**: Polyethylene T-shaped frame wrapped with fine copper wire or carrying copper sleeves.\n* **Mechanism of Action**:\n  * Copper ions are continuously released into the uterine cavity, acting as a highly effective **local spermicide**.\n  * They impair sperm motility, viability, and capacity to fertilize the ovum.\n  * They alter the endometrial lining, preventing blastocyst implantation.\n* **Key Models**:\n  * **Copper T 200**: Contains $200 \\text{ mm}^2$ of copper surface area. Effective for 3-4 years.\n  * **Copper T 380A**: The current global standard. Features **380 \\text{ mm}^2$ of copper** (sleeves on horizontal arms and wire on the vertical stem). **Effective for 10 years** of continuous protection.\n  * **Multiload 375 (ML-375)**: Features flexible, serrated side arms that cling to the uterine wall to minimize the risk of accidental expulsion. Effective for 5 years.\n\n#### 3. Third-Generation IUDs (Hormone-Releasing / Intrauterine Systems - IUS)\n* **Description**: T-shaped plastic frame carrying a reservoir that slowly and steadily releases a low daily dose of a progestin.\n* **Mechanism of Action**:\n  * The continuous release of hormone causes profound **endometrial atrophy**, making the endometrium completely unreceptive to implantation.\n  * It thickens the cervical mucus, creating a highly viscous barrier that blocks sperm penetration.\n  * It reduces menstrual blood loss and dysmenorrhea.\n* **Key Models**:\n  * **Mirena (LNG-20)**: Releases 20 mcg of **Levonorgestrel** daily. **Effective for 5 to 7 years**. Highly indicated as first-line treatment for menorrhagia (excessive menstrual bleeding) and dysmenorrhea.\n  * **Progestasert**: Releases natural progesterone; requires annual replacement.\n\n---\n\n### C) ADVANTAGES AND INDICATIONS\n* **Efficacy**: Extremely high efficacy ($>99\\%$), comparable to sterilization but completely reversible.\n* **Long-acting**: Provides continuous protection for 5 to 10 years depending on the model, without requiring daily user compliance.\n* **Cost-effective**: Free of cost in all public health facilities in India.\n* **Post-partum Insertion (PPIUD)**: Can be safely inserted within 48 hours of delivery, which is highly promoted under the National Health Mission.\n* **Emergency Contraception**: A copper IUD inserted within 5 days of unprotected intercourse is the most effective emergency contraceptive method.",
    "page": 26
